  "term": "rational emotive behavior therapy",
  "definition": "Rational emotive behavior therapy is a psychological therapy approach with a broad framework, theory, and application made up of fundamental processes. In this source, it is explained through the metaphor of the Hero’s Journey to help practitioners and clients understand how its parts fit together in practice.",
